// VARIANT ROTATION THIS ROUND, decided in .claude/brand-spec-ufabet168.md §3 and
// NOT re-picked here: the outgoing brand (โปรดี168) is rotated out of every family
// at once — Announcement3 replaces AnnouncementPremium, LatestWinners2 replaces
// LatestWinnersCyber, Faq2 replaces Faq4, ReviewCardSumo2 replaces the base
// ReviewCardSumo, and the ContentBox shape-mix drops FloatingBadge /
// 3ThreeCyberCut / Neumorphism / SevenThreeCyberCut / SevenThree (base) /
// TwoFloatingBadge for Premium / 3ThreePremium / CyberCut / SevenThreePremium /
// SevenThreeNeumorphism / TwoCyberCut — **zero file overlap with the outgoing
// brand's mix apart from the two pinned files below.** NavbarStyle9 + FooterCyber
// are the layout's pair this round and the brand font moves google-sans -> kanit;
// all of that is the orchestrator's shared-chrome step, not this page's.
// ⚠️ ContentBox.astro (the base) IS in this round's mix — it carries docx §6 — and it
// is also always-live shared chrome, because terms, privacy, 404, /promotion, /ทางเข้า
// and the button pages all render through it. The orchestrator owns and rethemes that
// file; **this page imports and uses it but never edits it.** An "is it used?" check
// has to match the bare filename rather than the components/ path, which is how a
// component reached only from another file got misread as inventory once.
// FeatureHighlights is the other repeat, and for the same kind of reason: it is the
// only component in the library that carries the shape "one H2 + three short
// sub-points", which this brief genuinely has.
// Every unused *Style / *Premium / *Cyber / *Huay / *CyberCut / *FloatingBadge sibling,
// the other Faq* and Announcement* files, the other LatestWinners* and ReviewCardSumo
// all stay on disk as inventory for the next brand — nothing was deleted, and the
// earlier brands' hues still inside them are expected drift.
//
// Nine widgets this template usually offers are deliberately absent, and they are named
// without their file extension on purpose because the playbook's "is this component
// live?" check is a bare-filename grep: ProviderGrid and ProviderGridPremium are out
// because this brief names NO game studio at all — it says "ค่ายเกมที่เปิดให้บริการจริง"
// and "ค่ายเว็บตรง100%" and never one name — BankStrip is out for the same reason on
// the banking side, since the brief names no bank and no wallet, GameRankingBoard has
// no ranking to carry, SmoothCarousel has no brief section asking for a carousel,
// LoginRtpSection is out because its RTP table would put an RTP figure on the page
// while §6 allows only the brief's own numbers (0.3%, 0.8%, 100%, 24ชม., 3 ขั้นตอน),
// and FeaturedGames / PopularGamesStrip / LottoGrid would all have to invent game or
// market names the brief never writes. This is NOT a lottery brand, so nothing here
// links to /ตรวจหวย or /แนวทาง either — both pages are parked in src/pages-disabled/.
//
// <Announcement /> runs bare on purpose: Announcement3's default message is this
// brand's copy, written from this brief by the orchestrator, and every sub-page calls it
// bare too — so passing an override here is exactly how the ticker ends up saying two
// different things on two pages of the same site.
//
// PALETTE — CANARY GOLD LEADING, CHROME SILVER SECOND, CREAM INK ON **DARK SURFACES**
// (brand-spec §2). ⚠️⚠️ **THIS ROUND GOES BACK TO A DARK THEME after three light-theme
// brands in a row** (รวยแท้168 ffdbdb, โปรดี168 ffd1d1). bg.json for this drop is
// {"mode":"color","color":"#000000"}, a pure black page background, and bg.json is the
// ONLY source of that value: do not inherit a light page from the last three rounds and
// do not "fix" it back to pastel. Every ContentBox*, FeatureHighlights, the FAQ, the
// winners feed and the review ledger therefore run DARK surfaces (#15130f raised /
// #1e1a13 warm / #0a0908 sunken) with CREAM ink (#eae3d4 = BRAND_TEXT, 14.6:1 on the
// card and 16.6:1 on black). Head and foot (NavbarStyle9, FooterCyber, Announcement3,
// Navfoot, CtaRedirect) are dark too this round, so the whole page is one dark field
// rather than a light body bracketed by dark chrome. **Do not "fix" any half of it.**
// Read off the artwork: the logo is a black-and-white football with gold panelling and
// a curved gold orbit tail, beside the Thai word ยูฟ้า in glossy 3-D canary gold,
